+      "claim": "Ferrous and non-ferrous metals can be reliably separated by magnetism.",
+      "truth": "Iron content defines the families; magnetism does not. Austenitic stainless steel is usually non-magnetic, while nickel is ferromagnetic despite containing no iron.",
+      "evidence": "Wikipedia, Stainless steel, Magnetism; Wikipedia, Nickel, magnetic ordering (fetched 2026-09-04).",
+      "verdict": "FIX"
