+      "id": "F3",
+      "lesson": 2,
+      "field": "conclusion_html",
+      "severity": "MEDIUM",
+      "claim": "Thermosetting plastics cannot be recycled.",
+      "truth": "Conventional thermosets cannot be re-melted or re-shaped after curing. That usually prevents recycling for the same use, but does not make all recycling impossible.",
+      "evidence": "Wikipedia, Thermosetting polymer, Properties, lines 165–169 (fetched 2026-09-04).",
+      "verdict": "FIX"
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "F4",
+      "lesson": 3,
+      "field": "content_html",
+      "severity": "MEDIUM",
+      "claim": "The stated list of ten specification properties splits conductivity into electrical and thermal conductivity, but omits environmental degradation.",
+      "truth": "The specification lists conductivity and environmental degradation among the ten properties. It does not split conductivity into electrical and thermal conductivity in that list.",
+      "evidence": "spec 3.2.2, lines 1768–1780.",
+      "verdict": "FIX"
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "F5",
+      "lesson": 4,
+      "field": "content_html",
+      "severity": "HIGH",
+      "claim": "Resistance is the inverse of conductivity.",
+      "truth": "Resistance depends on sample dimensions. Resistivity is calculated from resistance, length and cross-sectional area; conductivity is the reciprocal of resistivity.",
+      "evidence": "Wikipedia, Electrical resistivity and conductivity, lines 180–199 and 217–220 (fetched 2026-09-04).",
+      "verdict": "FIX"
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "F6",
+      "lesson": 4,
+      "field": "content_html",
+      "severity": "MEDIUM",
+      "claim": "The specification lists hardness testing under destructive testing.",
+      "truth": "The specification requires understanding of destructive and non-destructive testing for physical properties but does not assign hardness testing to either category. Hardness testing may be NDT when its indent has no harmful effect on the component.",
+      "evidence": "spec 3.2.3, lines 1789–1798; British Institute of NDT, About NDT, lines 568–570 (fetched 2026-09-04).",
